      "body": "Since the availability preflight runs before any blocks are rescanned, early notification registration can be dropped.\n\nThe race reproduces when blocks submitted prior to `loadwallet` are still being processed on the validation queue. In `AttachChain()`, `handleNotifications()` registers the wallet at line 3080 before checking block availability on disk. While `AttachChain()` holds `cs_wallet` during the `haveBlockOnDisk` backward scan, the scheduler picks up the in-flight block (height 357 in `wallet_assumeutxo.py`) and blocks on `cs_wallet`. Once `AttachChain()` fails and releases `cs_wallet`, the scheduler acquires the lock and `CWallet::blockConnected()` writes the height 357 locator to disk before `DisconnectChainNotifications()` finishes draining.\n\nOn subsequent load, the wallet trusts that locator and skips blocks 300–356. Deferring `handleNotifications()` until after the availability check passes prevents the failing load from registering:\n\n```diff\n--- a/src/wallet/wallet.cpp\n+++ b/src/wallet/wallet.cpp\n@@ -3080,2 +3080,0 @@ bool CWallet::AttachChain(...)\n-    walletInstance->m_chain_notifications_handler = walletInstance->chain().handleNotifications(walletInstance);\n-\n@@ -3147,0 +3148,2 @@ bool CWallet::AttachChain(...)\n+        walletInstance->m_chain_notifications_handler = walletInstance->chain().handleNotifications(walletInstance);\n+\n@@ -3168,0 +3171,2 @@ bool CWallet::AttachChain(...)\n+    } else {\n+        walletInstance->m_chain_notifications_handler = walletInstance->chain().handleNotifications(walletInstance);\n```",
