      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "A failed wallet load must not persist locator state to disk.\n\nFixing only the test leaves on-disk corruption reachable in production: whenever `AttachChain` aborts on pruned data or in-progress assumeutxo sync, drained callbacks from concurrent blocks can write a locator at tip. The write does not even require a relevant payment, since `blockConnected` triggers `WriteBestBlock()` periodically every 144 blocks regardless. On subsequent load, the wallet skips the missing historical range, silently omitting confirmed transactions.\n\nGating `blockConnected` and `blockDisconnected` on `m_is_attached` (set under `cs_wallet` upon successful return of `AttachChain`) ensures failed loads drop in-flight notifications without mutating disk.",
      "user": {
        "login": "Yudis-bit",
        "id": 85178972,
        "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjg1MTc4OTcy",
